ests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Michigan sits at the center of the electoral map as a genuinely even state, and the presidential contest there is best treated as a pure toss-up. The incumbent president is term-limited, so neither party starts with an incumbency edge, and the state's partisan lean is dead even. No public polls of the race, expert ratings, or market prices are available yet, leaving fundamentals to carry the estimate.\n\nRecent Michigan headlines describe a competitive 2026 Senate race, with national surrogates campaigning and prediction markets favoring the Democrat, which hints at Democratic energy in the state. But those signals belong to a different race and a midterm electorate, and Michigan's presidential vote has swung between the parties in consecutive cycles. With no race-specific evidence in hand, the contest holds at an even margin with wide uncertainty.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.4963, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.5203, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.4949, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.4948, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.4983, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.5, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.5029, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.504, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.5032, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.5003, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.5003, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.5026, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.5012, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.4979, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.493, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.5016, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.4999, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.5013, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.4984, "margin": 0.0}, {"date":